WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.245 --> 00:00:02.625
♫ Take you to the movies

00:00:02.625 --> 00:00:04.126
♫ Girl, we'll make the movie

00:00:04.126 --> 00:00:05.749
♫ How I fallin' back to the beat

00:00:05.749 --> 00:00:06.627
♫ I'm on a roll

00:00:06.627 --> 00:00:08.012
♫ Take on the world

00:00:08.012 --> 00:00:10.845
♫ Yes, yes, y'all

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:15.742
- [Sam] I work with Zulu P,

00:00:15.742 --> 00:00:20.006
and they are a rap group
here in New York City.

00:00:20.006 --> 00:00:23.008
They've played shows all
over New York at this point.

00:00:23.008 --> 00:00:26.193
The group consists of the
founding member Marley G.

00:00:26.193 --> 00:00:27.814
- I'm the great Marley G.

00:00:27.814 --> 00:00:29.009
- [Sam] Sweetness.

00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:31.608
♫ Like a sunshine

00:00:31.608 --> 00:00:32.441
- [Sam] T. Rock.

00:00:32.441 --> 00:00:33.274
♫ My microphone chill

00:00:33.274 --> 00:00:34.482
♫ Might overload it

00:00:34.482 --> 00:00:36.674
- [Sam] And Lil E.B.

00:00:36.674 --> 00:00:38.196
- All better and peace!

00:00:38.196 --> 00:00:41.863
They have a really
original take on hip-hop.

00:00:44.739 --> 00:00:47.115
We have a program here that serves adults

00:00:47.115 --> 00:00:51.493
with developmental disabilities
who also play music.

00:00:51.493 --> 00:00:54.499
They don't seem to develop preconceptions

00:00:54.499 --> 00:00:57.251
about how things should be.

00:00:57.251 --> 00:00:59.001
Definitely musically.

00:01:01.005 --> 00:01:03.777
It's a really striking
kind of freedom, I think,

00:01:03.777 --> 00:01:07.758
for people who live their
lives guided by and sometimes

00:01:07.758 --> 00:01:11.524
bounded by other people's
perceptions or preconceptions.

00:01:11.524 --> 00:01:13.857
(deep beat)

00:01:20.507 --> 00:01:22.255
- [Sam] We just book Zulu P on shows

00:01:22.255 --> 00:01:23.762
like you would book any regular band

00:01:23.762 --> 00:01:27.679
and don't give any type
of preface or anything.

00:01:29.232 --> 00:01:30.520
People will come.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.014
They'll see the show,

00:01:32.014 --> 00:01:34.259
but you can see that there's
a little tension there

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:35.243
for people.

00:01:35.243 --> 00:01:39.746
But I think it's a productive
and interesting tension.

00:01:39.746 --> 00:01:42.735
(audience applauds)

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:46.207
The members of Zulu P are completely open,

00:01:46.207 --> 00:01:49.489
totally positive, always down.

00:01:49.489 --> 00:01:53.246
They're not cynical, and
they're never self-conscious.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.691
- I'm Zulu P.

00:01:54.691 --> 00:01:56.005
Peace out.

00:01:56.005 --> 00:01:57.125
- [Sam] It's really amazing to see them

00:01:57.125 --> 00:01:59.625
get up there and crush a show.

